WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.400
Hey, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, Daily Episode 521. I'm Patrick in Vancouver. Today is June 24th, 2026. Let's dive into today's Tesla news.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:21.480
Cybertruck becomes the only 2026 pickup to earn IIHS Top Safety Pick Plus after avoiding every pedestrian collision in daytime and nighttime tests.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:31.940
Tesla reported that the Cybertruck avoided every collision in IIHS pedestrian front crash prevention tests across daytime, nighttime, and multiple angles.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:44.800
It was the sole pickup to receive the highest 2026 award. The result highlights how the vehicle's sensor suite and braking calibration performed under controlled conditions that replicate real world encounters.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:01:00.220
The IIHS rating provides an independent benchmark separate from NHTSA 5-star scores. Listeners should watch for whether the same hardware stack translates to unsupervised operation metrics later this year.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:08.780
While the Cybertruck shows strong safety hardware results, a look back at Tesla's early hardware decisions reveals how those foundations were built.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:21.600
The Fortune Profile details how Stravel's initial battery focus proposal was rejected before he reframed it as a side project that scaled into Tesla's core energy storage and powertrain business.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:33.800
The article traces the shift from early skepticism to the company's current valuation. It underscores how iterative hardware development at the cell level supported later vehicle programs.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:42.360
The piece also notes Stravel's subsequent work on redwood materials, which now recycles battery materials at industrial scale.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:53.140
From early company building stories to current analyst views on the stock, UBS maintained its hold rating without issuing a new price target in the latest note.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.340
The firm cited ongoing questions around vehicle margin trends and the timeline for new programs.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:05.580
The rating follows recent delivery data and does not reflect any shift in the bank's modeling assumptions.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:11.860
Investors will look to the next earnings call for updated guidance on energy storage and services revenue.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:17.800
Analysts caution on margins pairs with a closer look at real world repair economics.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:26.620
The report details how Tesla body panels and structural components carry higher replacement costs than comparable parts on legacy vehicles.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:34.740
Specific examples include front end assemblies and door modules that require specialized calibration after installation.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:42.600
The article notes that parts availability and certified repair networks influence total out of pocket expenses for owners.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.940
Higher repair costs can affect insurance premiums and long-term ownership calculations.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:53.440
Repair costs tie directly into the longer term ownership questions we explore next.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:03.340
Repair costs sit outside the usual efficiency and range conversations yet directly shape whether buyers repeat purchase or switch brands after the first incident.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:17.480
A front end module replacement that requires sensor recalibration and structural adhesive work can exceed the deductible on many policies, turning a minor parking lot tap into a several thousand dollar event.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:32.960
The same vertical integration that trims assembly labor also concentrates replacement part pricing power inside one supplier network so discounts available to high volume body shops on other Marques do not always appear here.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:42.860
Legacy manufacturers spread repair knowledge across thousands of independent shops that stock interchangeable panels and publish standardized labor times.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:54.820
Tesla's approach keeps proprietary calibration routines and part numbers inside its own ecosystem which speeds initial quality control but lengthens the tail of post collision logistics.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:04:04.180
Over a five-year ownership cycle the cumulative effect appears in residual values and insurance quotes rather than EPA window stickers.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:15.700
Ownership realities lead us to new vehicle testing sightings. A Tesla semi was photographed carrying additional sensor arrays consistent with autonomous validation hardware.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:22.420
The sighting occurred on public roads and suggest continued testing of the class eight trucks driver assistance stack.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:34.060
The driven reports no official comment from Tesla on deployment timelines observers will track whether the same hardware path used in passenger vehicles scales to the heavier platform.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:42.680
SpaceX confirmed star mind as the name for its planned AI satellite constellation aimed at one million orbital compute nodes.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:49.280
The system would place inference hardware directly in orbit rather than relying on terrestrial facilities.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:58.120
Tesla Roddy notes the architecture could reduce latency for certain workloads while shifting power and cooling demands away from ground-based sites.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:11.940
The announcement ties into broader plans for high bandwidth satellite links already used by Starlink. Elon Musk confirmed the orbital compute approach would make Earth data centers obsolete for targeted inference tasks.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:26.680
The constellation builds on existing Starlink infrastructure for data transmission between nodes no deployment timeline was provided in the initial announcement from commercial truck testing to passenger vehicle software updates.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:32.640
A driver recorded the software shifting lanes to accommodate a motorcycle overtaking on the highway.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:43.000
The behavior matched earlier community clips of similar courtesy maneuvers. The clip shows the system interpreting dynamic road users without explicit driver input.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:55.320
Owners note the action reduces the need for manual intervention and mixed traffic. The same software version read a right lane keep moving sign as applying to the exit lane and began breaking.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:04.460
The driver used the accelerator to override the incident illustrates how sign interpretation remains a variable and highway exit scenarios.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.700
Tesla Roddy posted the video for comparison with future point releases.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:14.720
Tesla Roddy flagged an imminent point release of the V14.3.4 branch.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:21.820
The post did not include change log details but signaled continued iteration on the current supervised stack.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:27.780
Owners tracking release cadence expect incremental fixes for edge cases seen in recent clips.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:38.060
The update path remains separate from any unsupervised regulatory timeline. Software behavior on the road connects to fresh model Y variants entering the lineup.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:46.580
Reports indicate Tesla is preparing a longer range model Y variant for the US to replace the departed model X in the lineup.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:57.080
The move would maintain a higher capacity option without reintroducing the older 3-row platform. No official confirmation or pricing details have been released.

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.800
The change would affect fleet and family buyers who previously chose the model X for range.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:10.620
The review examines the longer wheelbase model YL configured with 7 seats and priced near $80,000.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:17.040
The driven test real world space ride quality and efficiency on Australian roads.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:24.140
The video compares cargo flexibility against standard model Y variants and notes the added mass effect on range.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:30.460
Viewers can assess whether the stretch addresses family hauling needs without moving to a larger platform.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:36.840
The model YL adds a third row while retaining the core platform dimensions of the standard vehicle.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:46.880
Efficiency measurements in the review account for the extra seating and wheelbase stretch. No official Tesla confirmation accompanied the independent test footage.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:51.060
New model planning brings us to manufacturing and content rankings.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:58.120
The model 3 again led the annual American made index despite broader EV sales slowdowns.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:03.560
The ranking factors domestic content, assembly location and supplier geography.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:09.580
The article notes that two previously high ranking Tesla models dropped from the list this year.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:15.400
Continued leadership depends on sustained US production volumes at Fremont and Texas.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:23.800
A Reddit user observed that a pre-juniper model Y lacked the audible pedestrian warning present on other recent Tesla models.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:28.360
The post notes the absence even when standing directly beside the vehicle.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.180
The discussion raises questions about hardware revisions across production years.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:39.200
Owners may check their specific build dates if local regulations require minimum sound output.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:44.640
The observation came from direct testing in a quiet environment with the vehicle stationary.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:49.260
No Tesla response was posted in the thread regarding the specific build configuration.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:54.640
The thread prompted other owners to verify their own vehicles for the same trait.

00:08:55.340 --> 00:09:01.160
A Tesla entered a Beverly Hills playground area and caused damage in an incident captured on video.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:06.480
The New York Post reports no immediate details on driver status or vehicle mode.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.820
Local authorities are investigating the sequence of events.

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:15.860
Such events draw renewed attention to vehicle control systems in low speed urban settings.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:20.760
Video footage showed the vehicle crossing into the playground boundary before stopping.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:24.720
No injuries were reported in the initial coverage of the incident.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:31.180
Tesla is rolling the parked vehicle blind spot alert to additional models beyond the initial launch group.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:37.220
The feature uses ultrasonic and camera data to warn occupants before opening doors into traffic.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:44.620
Not a Tesla app notes the update improves protection for both vehicle occupants and passing cyclists or pedestrians.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:49.620
The expansion follows software validation on earlier hardware variants.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:55.900
The alert activates when the vehicle is stationary and detects approaching objects on either side.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.660
Rollout timing varies by software branch and vehicle configuration.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:08.880
A user asks for detailed logs of Denver to Las Vegas routes including specific charge point and supercharger locations.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:13.800
Respondents shared sequences of stops with measured times and energy added.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:19.320
The discussion highlights how current network density affects planning for Western US travel.

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:24.320
The thread offers practical data points beyond manufacturing range estimates.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:30.260
Multiple participants posted exact kilowatt hours figures and dwell times at each charger.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:35.760
Root variations included both major corridors and secondary stops for flexibility.

